# Cisco One Experience Lab — local memory

dCloud **PseudoCo / Cisco One** lab. Client VPN must be up before SSH or playbooks. Topology lives in `Lab Topology/`. The single credential source for every playbook is vault-encrypted `Lab Topology/lab_access.yml`, unlocked by the repo-root gitignored `.vault`. The markdown lookup is an index of hosts and URLs only. Do not put passwords in playbooks or unencrypted inventory.

## Workflow

- Author playbooks on the Mac in this repo. Do not write new playbooks on Kali.
- Commit/push only when the user asks. Remote: `https://github.com/imanassypov/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation` (`main`, public).
- Test on the Kali script server after it has `main` at `~/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation`.
- Mac refresh (VPN up): `ansible-automation/00_scriptserver_bootstrap` venv, then `playbooks/01_bootstrap_script_server.yml` (also git-pulls) or `playbooks/02_sync_from_git.yml` (git only). Kali tree is often dirty from ad-hoc file copies; `02` fails until those are committed or reverted.
- On Kali, Ansible is on PATH from `~/venv`. Recreate the repo-root `.vault` there after clone (gitignored). One line only, same password as the Mac.
- Run CatC stages from Mac via `00_scriptserver_bootstrap` `.venv` → `ansible script_server -m shell` in `~/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation/ansible-automation/01_campus/evpn/ansible`. Copy Mac-only edits to Kali first when git is stale.

## Script server

- Kali Linux at `198.18.134.12`. SSH user and password come from `lab_access.script_server` in `Lab Topology/lab_access.yml`. Bootstrap sets resolver to lab DNS `198.18.5.102` (fallback `198.18.128.1`) so `corp.pseudoco.com` names resolve.
- Mac controller: project `.venv` via `setup-local-venv.sh`; `ansible_connection: paramiko`.
- Only project tree on Kali: `~/cisco-one-experience-lab-automation`. Never create `~/cisco-one-automation`.

## Collections

- Playbooks live under `ansible-automation/`, numbered by lab-build order: `00_scriptserver_bootstrap`, `01_campus`, `02_data_center`, `03_dmz`, `04_remote_dc`, `05_sdwan`, `06_secure_access`.
- Inside each collection, playbooks are `00_`, `01_`, … in apply order.
- `01_campus` has two independent tracks: `sda/` (stub) and `evpn/` (Site 105).
- EVPN is **Catalyst Center GitOps**, not a `cisco.ios` underlay/overlay pusher. Fabric CLI is rendered by CatC from vendored Jinja DEFN/FUNC/FABRIC templates (`evpn/Catalyst Center Templates/`). The only playbook collection is `evpn/ansible/` (CICD `00`–`09`, verify `10`). Settings SSOT is `evpn/Settings/`. CatC API credentials come from `lab_access['Catalyst Center']`. Site 105 verify uses `lab_access[inventory_hostname]`.
- Live CatC is **3.1.5**. Ansible/SDK API profile is **3.1.3.0** (SDK has no `3.1.5` string). Pins: `cisco.catalystcenter` 2.10.2, `cisco.dnac` 6.46.0, `catalystcentersdk` 3.1.3.0.1, `dnacentersdk` 2.10.6. Do not drop `cisco.catalystcenter` below 2.4.0.
- `template_source: local`. `template_local_root` is `evpn/` (two dirnames up from `playbooks/`). Subfolder `Catalyst Center Templates/Site BGP EVPN Templates` → CatC project **Site-105**. Composite `BGP-EVPN-BUILD.j2`.
- `10_verify_collect_facts.yml` = `ios_command` on `198.18.128.22–24` → `ansible/evidence/` on the host that ran the play (Kali if driven from the script server). It does **not** build the fabric.
- `settings.json` matches live CatC hierarchy (state → city → building → MAIN). Four project rows: DC-Site-10 (WLC `198.18.5.103`, `C9800-WLC`, `HQ-Switching`), DC-Site-11 (empty, `Remote-DC-Switching`), Site-105 (`.1–.3`, `Site-105-Discovery`, no NETCONF, `BGP-EVPN-Switching`, Day-N `BGP-EVPN-BUILD.j2`), Site-106 (empty, `Branch-Switching`). DEFN hostname keys MUST match CatC `__device.hostname` (inventory name): `Site_105-Leaf1|Leaf2|Border-Spine.corp.pseudoco.com` (IOS hostname + `ip domain name`, not `.dcloud.cisco.com`). ASN 65535, VRFs Main/PROD/IOT. Border-Spine is SPINE+RR+BORDER; leaves CLIENT only.
- Source of the vendored trees: `imanassypov/CatalystCenter-BGP-EVPN-VXLAN` `6d2afa3a2becfe71f8f036ee79a0a1c164ba0433`.
- `00_` is implemented. `01_campus/evpn` has the CatC pipeline vendored. Other `01_`–`06_` tracks are stubs.

## Pipeline (as of 2026-09-02)

- Pruned to `00`–`10`. Deleted: the SWIM `06.x` series with `roles/swim` + `roles/http_image_server` + `image_servers` inventory; `deploy_yangsuite.yml` with `roles/yangsuite_docker` + `yangsuite_servers`; the config backup stage with `roles/backup_configs`, `config-backups/`, `group_vars/iosxe|nxos`, `inventory/cml.yml` and `platform_groups.yml`; and the verify preflight play. Survivors were renumbered to close the gaps. Stage numbers below use the new scheme.
- Inventory is now `static_inventory.yml` only — two groups, `catalyst_center` (localhost → CatC API, stages `01`–`09`) and `campus_evpn` (three switches over SSH, stage `10`). No CML, no `.env`. `cisco.cml`/`cisco.nxos`/`virl2_client` dropped from the evpn requirements files.
- Ran on Kali: `01`–`05`, `06`–`09`, and the verify play. Do not re-run `08`/`09` against the live lab until asked.
- `01`: skip building/floor UPDATE (`site_hierarchy_update_existing: false`). `cisco.catalystcenter.buildings` PUT raises `UnboundLocalError: local variable 'func'`. Re-enable with `-e site_hierarchy_update_existing=true`.
- `03`: bind live Design names, do not CREATE duplicates. Live: CLI `CLI Admin`, SNMP `SNMPv2c Read`/`SNMPv2c Write`, NETCONF `defaultNetConfPort` (830), HTTP `HTTPS Read`/`HTTPS Write`. Each project row `assign_credentials.site_name` = that site’s MAIN path.
- `08`: three passes. `POST /dna/intent/api/v1/sda/provisionDevices` cannot set wireless DeviceInfo (`NCWL10092`). `roles/provision_devices/tasks/provision_site.yml` defers `family` containing `Wireless` to `provision_wireless.yml`, which provisions the WLC and sets its managed AP locations. `provision_accesspoints.yml` then names and site-assigns APs. Site-105 9300s provisioned 3/3. The WLC pass is a no-op once provisioned — `force_provisioning` comes from `force_reprovision` (false), and the module short-circuits on "already provisioned" without diffing intent, so a changed `managed_ap_locations` needs `-e force_reprovision=true`. Gates: `wireless_provision_enabled`, `ap_provision_enabled`.
- CatC cannot set an AP policy/site tag directly and `accesspoint_workflow_manager` has no field for either. Tags are derived from the site: assign the AP to a site bound to a wireless profile and CatC generates and pushes them. No site ⇒ `default-policy-tag` ⇒ AP broadcasts nothing.
- AP MAC gotcha: CatC indexes an AP by **radio** MAC (`macAddress`), not Ethernet (`apEthernetMacAddress`). `?macAddress=<eth>` returns 0 devices and the module resolves APs through that same query. `lab_ap_macs` holds the Ethernet MAC (what the student can read); `provision_accesspoints.yml` lists `family=Unified AP` and translates. Site-105-AP-1: eth `04:5f:b9:ca:03:58` → radio `68:7d:b4:90:95:00`.
- Live WLC `198.18.5.103` as of 2026-09-03 (note: `lab_access['C9800-WLC']` says `.102`, which is wrong — `.102` is DNS/AD): WLAN 1 `DCLOUD-XAR-FLEX-Profile` SSID `PSEUDOCO-POD#` (dCloud pre-built, never renamed) and WLAN 17 `PSEUDOCO-FLEX-Profile` SSID `PSEUDOCO-POD12` (pushed by our stage 07). Pre-built tags `DCLOUD-XAR-FLEX-PT`/`FLEX-SITE` exist but CatC created none of its own. AP `SITE-105-AP-1` is Registered, already named, location `Leaf1`, `siteHierarchy: None`, on all three default tags. Going CatC-native means the AP ends up on CatC-generated tags serving `PSEUDOCO-POD12`; the dCloud WLAN and tags stay dormant.
- `09` queues only `DayNTemplateNames` with `DeployTemplate: true`. Site-105 was flipped to `true` so the play would not assert-empty. CatC reported SUCCESS (`5d38a5da-561e-40fa-b00b-563ef5ab4eab`) for `172.30.255.1–3`.
- `10` verify after that push: underlay is up (Loopback0, OSPF FULL). Overlay is **not** on the boxes: `% BGP not active`, no NVE peers, VRF `Mgmt-vrf` only, no Main/PROD/IOT. CatC deploy SUCCESS ≠ CLI present.

## CatC Jinja UDV scanner

- Static scan ignores `{% set %}` inside `{% for %}`. Dummy-declare loop vars at template scope (already done for `vrf`).
- `default((L3VNIOFFSET|string) + vrf.id)` does not parse as a declaration. Bare `{{ l3_vni }}` becomes a required Template Hub input (“Value should not be empty”).
- Site-105 `DEFN-VRF.j2` already has explicit `l3_vlan` / `l3_vni`. Prefer `{{ vrf['l3_vni'] }}` over a local `l3_vni`. `FABRIC-NVE.j2` was fixed locally; **not yet re-synced with `06`**.
